diff --git a/docs/spec/codeplug-settings.md b/docs/spec/codeplug-settings.md
index 6b8437b..190b971 100644
--- a/docs/spec/codeplug-settings.md
+++ b/docs/spec/codeplug-settings.md
@@ -371,3 +371,13 @@ startup screen when the record is absent or a different length. This asset
 also appears in the startup screen preview. Diagnostics and firmware update
 screens retain their own banners. The editor stores or removes it with the
 rest of the settings area, preserving unrelated entries.
+
+The DM-32UV also stores a 128 × 128 indexed color splash at EEPROM image
+offset `0xB000`, outside the settings sector and the qdmr transfer ranges.
+The record starts with `RFB1`, the CRC-32 of the legacy 1,024-byte image,
+and the CRC-32 of the color payload (both little-endian). The payload is
+16 little-endian RGB565 palette entries and 8,192 pixel bytes, in row order
+with the higher nibble first. The first palette entry fills the letterbox.
+The radio uses the legacy image if either CRC fails, including after a partial
+write or a legacy CPS change. The CPS transfers the color record only when the
+radio advertises `SPLASH_COLOR`. Full CPS file exports include both records.
